Chapter: ProbeClosureSolo

 The known-good cell, alone in its own chapter. `make-adder` and one
 driver line, nothing else defined.

 This exists to test INTERFERENCE. The same expression printed 47 in
 probe-closure-return.codex, where a faulting definition was also
 present, but faulted as the FIRST line of probe-closure-saturated.codex,
 where a different faulting definition was present. If it prints 47 here,
 then a bad definition elsewhere in the chapter can break a good one, and
 the damage is not confined to the definition that causes it.

Section: Shapes

  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (x) (y) (z) = x + y + z

  make-adder : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  make-adder (n) = add3 n

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("solo " & show (((make-adder 5) 20) 22))
  end
